# 203 - Drop All Creatures Except Spirit Healers

**Phase:** 2 (Empty World)
**Effect:** World is truly empty, only spirit healers and critters remain
**Status:** Completed (2026-04-06)

---

## The Effect

The world database contains no static creature spawns except:
- **Spirit healers** (required for resurrection)
- **Critters** (ambient animals like rabbits, squirrels)

All other NPCs removed. The world is empty by default—monsters only spawn via the ambush system, travelers wander dynamically, treasure appears randomly.

This is the empty canvas for the roguelike survival experience.

---

## What This Solved

### Before (Populated World)

**Default AzerothCore creature spawns:**
- Thousands of static NPCs in every zone
- Quest givers, vendors, guards, monsters
- Predictable positions and respawn patterns
- World feels like traditional MMO

**Conflicts with roguelike design:**
- Static creatures compete with ambush system
- Players expect traditional quest chains
- Predictability undermines survival theme
- World doesn't feel empty or dangerous

### After (Empty World)

**Creatures removed:**
- All quest givers (no traditional quests)
- All vendors (custom merchant system planned - issue 135)
- All static monsters (replaced by ambush spawns)
- All guards, trainers, flavor NPCs

**Creatures kept:**
- Spirit healers (resurrection mechanic)
- Critters (ambient life, harmless)

**Result:**
- World feels abandoned and mysterious
- No guidance, must explore to survive
- Encounters are dynamic (ambush), not static
- Aligns with roguelike philosophy

